Task #743: Show bundle size changes as a sticky PR comment

Added a new GitHub Actions workflow that runs the bundle size gate on
every pull request to main and posts (or updates) a single sticky
comment summarizing total JS, main chunk, and per-pillar deltas vs the
main baseline.

Changes:
- easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/scripts/bundle-size-gate.ts
  - appendSummary() now also writes the markdown body to the path in
    BUNDLE_SIZE_COMMENT_FILE (in addition to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY) so
    the workflow can reuse the existing markdown table as a PR comment.
- easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/.github/workflows/bundle-size-gate.yml (new)
  - Runs on pull_request to main with pull-requests: write permission.
  - Checks out with fetch-depth: 0 and fetches origin/main so the
    script can resolve the baseline from BUNDLE_SIZE_BASELINE_REF.
  - Installs deps, builds, runs `npm run bundle:gate` with
    BUNDLE_SIZE_COMMENT_FILE pointed at the workspace root.
  - Uses marocchino/sticky-pull-request-comment@v2 with
    header: bundle-size-gate so each push updates the same comment
    instead of duplicating it.
  - continue-on-error on the gate step plus a follow-up step that
    re-fails the job ensures the comment is still posted when the
    gate fails.

Notes / deviations:
- The task description referenced an existing bundle-size-gate.yml,
  but only the script existed in the repo; the workflow has been
  created from scratch following the patterns in deploy-now.yml.

